    <briefdescription>
<para><computeroutput>Frobby::IdealConsumer</computeroutput> adapter that collects Frobby&apos;s output monomials into an engine <computeroutput><ref refid="class_monomial_ideal" kindref="compound">MonomialIdeal</ref></computeroutput>. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>Holds a scratch <computeroutput><ref refid="class_my_ideal_consumer_a9fa6a0880d1ee5811e2b73f0aafe6895_1a9fa6a0880d1ee5811e2b73f0aafe6895" kindref="member">exp</ref></computeroutput> buffer of length <computeroutput><ref refid="class_my_ideal_consumer_a604ce706effcc4356f09c6ab9a657e70_1a604ce706effcc4356f09c6ab9a657e70" kindref="member">nv</ref></computeroutput> (the variable count) and a <computeroutput>MonomialIdeal* <ref refid="class_my_ideal_consumer_acda050bce435f9059d889444d1278af6_1acda050bce435f9059d889444d1278af6" kindref="member">J</ref></computeroutput> accumulator. Each <computeroutput><ref refid="class_my_ideal_consumer_ab268ff4b12d3b60acf510e207d63dcb4_1ab268ff4b12d3b60acf510e207d63dcb4" kindref="member">consume</ref></computeroutput> callback from Frobby converts the incoming <computeroutput>mpz_t**</computeroutput> exponent vector into engine <computeroutput><ref refid="class_my_ideal_consumer_a9fa6a0880d1ee5811e2b73f0aafe6895_1a9fa6a0880d1ee5811e2b73f0aafe6895" kindref="member">exp</ref></computeroutput> form and appends it to <computeroutput><ref refid="class_my_ideal_consumer_acda050bce435f9059d889444d1278af6_1acda050bce435f9059d889444d1278af6" kindref="member">J</ref></computeroutput>. The completed ideal is then handed back to the front end as the result of the Frobby-backed monomial operation. </para>
    </detaileddescription>
